### MC6800 port of SDCC

This fork adds support for the Motorola MC6800 to SDCC.

In the last full regression run in uCsim, all `--stack-auto` tests passed.
The default build failed two tests on calls through function pointers.
CoreMark passed in both modes.

### Build from Git

```sh
git clone --branch mc6800 https://github.com/zu2/sdcc-6800.git
cd sdcc-6800

./configure \
	--disable-mcs51-port \
	--disable-z80-port \
	--disable-z180-port \
	--disable-r2k-port \
	--disable-r2ka-port \
	--disable-r3ka-port \
	--disable-r4k-port \
	--disable-r5k-port \
	--disable-r6k-port \
	--disable-sm83-port \
	--disable-tlcs90-port \
	--disable-ez80-port \
	--disable-z80n-port \
	--disable-r800-port \
	--disable-ds390-port \
	--disable-ds400-port \
	--disable-pic14-port \
	--disable-pic16-port \
	--enable-hc08-port \
	--disable-s08-port \
	--disable-stm8-port \
	--enable-mc6800-port \
	--disable-pdk13-port \
	--disable-pdk14-port \
	--disable-pdk15-port \
	--disable-pdk16-port \
	--disable-mos6502-port \
	--disable-mos65c02-port \
	--disable-huc6280-port \
	--disable-f8-port \
	--disable-f8l-port

make SVN_REVISION=0
```

The build also creates `sdas6800`, `sdld6800`, and `ucsim_m6800`.

The build uses 0 for `__SDCC_REVISION` because a Git commit in this
fork may have no SVN revision.

### Run the regression tests

Run both test suites from the source directory after the build:

```sh
make -C support/regression test-mc6800 test-mc6800-stack-auto
```

### Install

```sh
make install SVN_REVISION=0
```

The default install directory is `/usr/local`. To install in your home
directory, add `--prefix="$HOME/.local"` to the configure command.

